{"dossier":"D15","entry_points":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_write","fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_show","fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_set_timerslack_ns_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_read","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_write","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_operations","fs/proc/base.c::do_io_accounting","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tid_io_accounting","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tgid_io_accounting","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_ksm_merging_pages","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_ksm_stat","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_personality","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_patch_state","fs/proc/base.c::proc_stack_depth"],"text":"Timer slack, core filter, I/O, KSM, personality, patch and stack reports are small files resolving the target from the inode, with group I/O aggregating when flagged."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_instantiate","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_read","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_write","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tgid_base_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tgid_base_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tgid_base_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tgid_base_inode_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_id_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_setgroups_open"],"text":"Per-process directories share instantiate, lookup and enumerate helpers with cache splicing. Security attributes serve security-layer buffers. Group directory reuses table helpers with permission checks."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_instantiate","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_instantiate","fs/proc/fd.c::seq_fdinfo_open"],"text":"Process and thread lookup builds immutable directories after decimal, namespace and membership checks. Descriptor info open creates a single-entry sequential view."},{"sids":["fs/proc/bootconfig.c::saved_boot_config","fs/proc/bootconfig.c::boot_config_proc_show","fs/proc/bootconfig.c::proc_boot_config_init","fs/proc/cmdline.c::cmdline_proc_show","fs/proc/cmdline.c::proc_cmdline_init","fs/proc/consoles.c::show_console_dev","fs/proc/consoles.c::c_start","fs/proc/consoles.c::c_next","fs/proc/consoles.c::c_stop","fs/proc/consoles.c::consoles_op","fs/proc/consoles.c::proc_consoles_init","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_show","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_start","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_next","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_stop","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_ops","fs/proc/devices.c::proc_devices_init","fs/proc/cpuinfo.c::cpuinfo_open","fs/proc/cpuinfo.c::cpuinfo_proc_ops","fs/proc/cpuinfo.c::proc_cpuinfo_init","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_create","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_create_data","include/linux/proc_fs.h::proc_create_seq.alt_1","include/linux/proc_fs.h::proc_create_seq.alt_2"],"text":"Boot config and command line print saved snapshots, consoles list with flags and numbers, devices show per-major ranges, cpuinfo opens an arch view, with permanent marking and sequential creation helpers."},{"sids":["fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_lookupfdinfo","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_readdir_de","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_open","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_release","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_ops","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_single_open"],"text":"Descriptor lookups delegate to a common helper with type constructors, iteration resolves live files per number. Generic paths enforce process-only mode. Sequential open and release choose private or shared by size."}],"exports":[{"sids":["fs/proc/generic.c::proc_symlink","fs/proc/generic.c::_proc_mkdir","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_create_mount_point","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_mkdir_data","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_mkdir_mode","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_mkdir","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_single_open","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_set_size","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_get_parent_data","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_remove","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_entry","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_subtree"],"text":"Symlink, directory and mount-point creation under a parent with mkdir wrappers, single-shot binding, plus size, parent-data access and single or subtree removal."},{"sids":["fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup_de","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_readdir_de","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_get_inode","fs/proc/generic.c::pde_put","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_lookupfdinfo","fs/seq_file.c::seq_open_private","fs/seq_file.c::seq_release_private","fs/proc/base.c::proc_flush_pid","fs/proc/base.c::tgid_pidfd_to_pid","fs/seq_file.c::single_release"],"text":"Shared lookup, listing, inode build and release for generic entries, descriptor permission tables, private sequential open and release, pid flush, group to pid conversion and single release."}],"extracts":["44d0c4987203c940d5885b34941b2cd6b0b86f014a8cfb58671379a34fc4a545","8869e5c5845292e198643c3e2c748ea65102c4e648c8b6661e9be11f220261d7","9c5b8c68b43c8363b0b84e7b008793f6a90f6aaca7f48a9445fb9a794a8b4b72"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_write","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_read","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_write","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_id_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_setgroups_open","fs/proc/base.c::first_tid","fs/proc/bootconfig.c::proc_boot_config_init","init/main.c::cmdline_has_extra_options"],"text":"Resolution fails cleanly when the target exited. Numeric writes leave state untouched on parse failure. Thread start handles truncation; boot failures propagate without registration. Extra command checks extra storages."},{"sids":["fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_entry","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_subtree","fs/proc/internal.h::pde_is_permanent","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_get_inode","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_symlink","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup_de"],"text":"Removing permanent entries warns without change or fails; non-empty removal warns about leaked children. Allocation failure reports missing or out of memory; unknown types trap."},{"sids":["fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_misc_d_revalidate"],"text":"RCU validation must handle retry without blocking; missing tasks surface as search or missing entry. Counting and iteration tolerate exit by resolving per number."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_write","fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_show"],"text":"Own slack is always adjustable; foreign access needs scheduling privilege plus security approval. Real-time and deadline tasks pin to zero; writing zero restores the inherited default."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pident_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_instantiate","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_instantiate","fs/proc/base.c::next_tid","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_getattr","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tid_comm_permission","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tid_comm_inode_operations"],"text":"Process and thread lookup needs decimal form, namespace presence, membership and hide policy. Listings emit dots first then numeric ids in order, skipping hidden or exited tasks."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_write","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_read","fs/proc/base.c::proc_coredump_filter_write","fs/proc/base.c::do_io_accounting","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_ksm_stat","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_personality","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_patch_state","fs/proc/base.c::proc_stack_depth","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_ksm_merging_pages"],"text":"Attribute writes are opener-only, self-only, unoverridden, offset zero and single page. Core filter shows masked hex and updates per bit. I/O has seven fixed counters. KSM adds yes or no flags."},{"sids":["fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_get_inode","fs/proc/internal.h::pde_has_proc_read_iter","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_readdir_de","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_setattr","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup_de","fs/proc/fd.h::__PROCFS_FD_H__"],"text":"Descriptor names need decimal form with a live file; owner and mode refresh from task and open mode. Inode build copies only nonzero fields; process-only mode disables generic lookup and listing. Header uses a guard."},{"sids":["fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_open","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_release","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_ops","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_single_open","fs/proc/bootconfig.c::copy_xbc_key_value_list","fs/proc/base.c::proc_dir_llseek","fs/read_write.c::generic_llseek_cookie","fs/proc/base.c::set_proc_pid_nlink","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_inode_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/base.c::tid_base_stuff","fs/proc/internal.h::pde_make_permanent","fs/proc/bootconfig.c::rest","fs/seq_file.c::seq_pad","include/linux/seq_file.h::seq_setwidth"],"text":"Sequential open uses private state iff nonzero size is advertised. Boot rendering quotes values and appends extras. Cookie seek validates size and max; link counts derive from tables. Padding and capacity helpers support output."}],"locks":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_write","fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_show","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_attr_write","fs/proc/base.c::do_io_accounting","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_personality","fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_ksm_stat"],"text":"Foreign slack, attribute identity and group I/O use read-side protection; slack, personality, attribute, KSM and I/O use task, trace, credential-guard, mmap and exec-update locks with ptrace check."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::next_tgid","fs/proc/base.c::first_tid","fs/proc/base.c::next_tid","fs/proc/consoles.c::show_console_dev","fs/proc/consoles.c::c_start","fs/proc/consoles.c::c_stop"],"text":"Pid translation holds read-side protection only across lookup with a task reference dropped on all paths. Console mapping uses global lock narrowly while traversal holds list lock."},{"sids":["fs/proc/generic.c::proc_subdir_lock","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup_de","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_readdir_de","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_entry","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_subtree","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_entry_rundown","fs/proc/inode.c::close_pdeo","fs/proc/internal.h::pde_get","fs/proc/generic.c::pde_put","fs/proc/generic.c::pde_erase"],"text":"Child tree uses a dedicated rwlock, dropping across emission with extra reference. Descriptor sampling uses task plus RCU. Teardown uses biased count with completion and unload lock; entries use get and put."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p10","crown":"A","phase":"F5"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_id_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_id_map_release","fs/proc/base.c::proc_uid_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_gid_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_projid_map_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_setgroups_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_setgroups_release","fs/proc/base.c::proc_setgroups_operations"],"text":"Identity maps take a namespace reference at open, publish it via sequential private area, and drop it at release; setgroups write-open needs admin privilege in that namespace."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::make_tgid_iter","fs/proc/base.c::next_tgid","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::first_tid","fs/proc/base.c::next_tid"],"text":"Group scan starts one below start and adopts each next existing leader with a new reference. Thread listing emits dots, resumes from cached id and saves first unemitted id on full."},{"sids":["fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_misc_d_revalidate","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_dir_operations","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_lookup_de","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_entry","fs/proc/generic.c::remove_proc_subtree","fs/proc/inode.c::proc_entry_rundown","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_readdir_de"],"text":"Descriptor validation retries in RCU context, invalidates when task or file is gone, else refreshes. Misc dentries track usage sign, network always revalidates. Removal erases, runs rundown and releases; permanent aborts."}],"structs":[{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_pid_set_timerslack_ns_operations","fs/proc/base.c::timerslack_ns_open","fs/proc/base.c::proc_uid_map_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_gid_map_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_projid_map_operations","fs/proc/base.c::LSM_DIR_OPS","fs/proc/base.c::smack_attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::apparmor_attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::proc_attr_dir_readdir","fs/proc/base.c::proc_attr_dir_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_attr_dir_lookup","fs/proc/base.c::proc_attr_dir_inode_operations"],"text":"Timer slack uses single-shot sequential helpers with custom open and write. Identity maps share read, seek and release with per-type open and write. Each security module gets a generated attribute directory."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::tgid_base_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::tgid_iter"],"text":"Group catalog defines task, descriptor, map, namespace and network subdirectories plus many gated files. Thread iterator state is current number plus optional task reference plus namespace."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::proc_tid_base_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_tid_base_inode_operations","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_inode_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/base.c::proc_task_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/consoles.c::consoles_op","fs/proc/devices.c::devinfo_ops","fs/proc/cpuinfo.c::cpuinfo_proc_ops","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_dir_operations","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_dir_inode_operations","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_misc_d_revalidate","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_setattr","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_lookupfdinfo","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_seq_ops","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_subdir_lock","fs/proc/generic.c::pde_subdir_first"],"text":"Inode tables bind lookup with getattr and permission, file tables bind directory read with iteration and seek. Descriptor instantiation carries number plus observed mode; links resolve live paths, with sibling stepping."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::smack_attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::apparmor_attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::attr_dir_stuff","fs/proc/base.c::tgid_base_stuff","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fdinfo_permission","fs/proc/fd.c::proc_fd_permission","fs/proc/generic.c::proc_symlink","fs/proc/generic.c::_proc_mkdir","fs/proc/generic.c::PROC_DYNAMIC_FIRST"],"text":"Attribute modes are 0666 except previous 0444 and module subdirs 0555; task subdir 0555, descriptor and map subdirs 0500, slack 0666. Links report 64 bytes; dynamic numbers start at 0xF0000000."},{"sids":["fs/proc/base.c::do_io_accounting","fs/proc/consoles.c::show_console_dev","fs/proc/base.c::TGID_OFFSET"],"text":"I/O lines are rchar, wchar, syscr, syscw, read_bytes, write_bytes and cancelled_write_bytes. Console flags use E, C, B, N, p, b, a and R, W, U. Numeric entries start two beyond base."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/linux/err.h::ERR_PTR","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/sched/task.h::put_task_struct","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D01"},{"sid":"include/linux/fortify-string.h::strlen","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/completion.h::DECLARE_COMPLETION_ONSTACK.alt_1","state":"stub","target_do